DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioButtons.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$rb1 = RadioButtons(
    [
        [
            'Age of buyers',
            'Buyers of Domestic cars',
            'Buyers of imported cars'
        ],
        'None of the above'
    ],
    0,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

$rb2 = RadioButtons(
    [
        [
            'Buyers of new domestic cars and buyers of new imported cars',
            'Age of buyers of new domestic cars and age of buyers of new imported cars.',
            'Cars and buyers.'
        ],
        'None of the above'
    ],
    0,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML
Suppose we were comparing the mean age of buyers of new domestic cars to the mean age of buyers of new imported cars.

1. What is the variable under consideration?

    [_]{$rb1}

2. What are the two populations under consideration?

    [_]{$rb2}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
1. [$rb1]

2. [$rb2]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.